<title>USA: Chevron in $650 mln Saudi joint venture.</title>
<headline>Chevron in $650 mln Saudi joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>SAN RAMON, Calif. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chevron Corp's Chevron Chemical Co and Saudi Industrial Venture Capital Group said Tuesday they formed a 50-50 joint venture company to build and operate a $650 million petrochemical complex in Al-Jubail, Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p>In a statement, Chevron said the company will be known as Saudi Chevron Petrochemical, a Limited Liability Partnership.</p>
<p>Construction of a greenfield 480,000 ton-per-year benzene plant and a 220,000 ton-per-year cyclohexane unit is scheduled to be completed in mid-1999.</p>
<p>The plant will manufacture benzene from a natural gasoline feedstock supplied by Saudi Aramco.</p>
</text>
